{"schemaVersion":1,"generatedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","id":"37272d44598e3feceb024971","canonicalUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260813081452.4289-1-antoniu.miclaus%40analog.com/","channels":["linux-devicetree"],"thread":{"schemaVersion":1,"id":"thread:lore-git:20260813081452.4289-1-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com","source":{"kind":"static-generated","canonicalThreadUrl":"https://lore.kernel.org/r/20260813081452.4289-1-antoniu.miclaus%40analog.com/","fetchedAt":"2026-08-16T16:20:46.501Z","contentDigest":"lore-git:20260813081452.4289-1-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 3/3] iio: accel: adxl367: add support for INT2 interrupt pin","messages":{"20260816013936.01f135dc@jic23-huawei":{"id":"20260816013936.01f135dc@jic23-huawei","messageId":"20260816013936.01f135dc@jic23-huawei","references":["20260813081452.4289-1-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com","20260813081452.4289-4-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"],"missingAncestorIds":["20260813081452.4289-4-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com","20260813081452.4289-1-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"],"author":{"name":"Jonathan Cameron","address":"jic23@kernel.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Antoniu Miclaus","address":"antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Marcelo Schmitt","address":"marcelo.schmitt@analog.com"},{"name":"Nuno Sá","address":"nuno.sa@analog.com"},{"name":"Michael Hennerich","address":"Michael.Hennerich@analog.com"},{"name":"David Lechner","address":"dlechner@baylibre.com"},{"name":"Rob Herring","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Krzysztof Kozlowski","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Conor Dooley","address":"conor+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-iio@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T00:39:36.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T00:39:36.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 3/3] iio: accel: adxl367: add support for INT2 interrupt pin","mailingLists":[{"id":"devicetree.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"devicetree.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:14:52 +0300\nAntoniu Miclaus <antoniu.miclaus@analog.com> wrote:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"The ADXL367 provides two independent interrupt output pins, INT1 and"},{"depth":1,"text":"INT2, each with its own event mapping register (INTMAP1_LOWER at 0x2A"},{"depth":1,"text":"and INTMAP2_LOWER at 0x2B) sharing an identical bit layout. Until now"},{"depth":1,"text":"the driver hardcoded INT1 for all interrupt mappings, so a board that"},{"depth":1,"text":"routes only INT2 to the host could never receive activity, inactivity"},{"depth":1,"text":"or FIFO watermark interrupts."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Determine the connected pin from the interrupt-names device tree"},{"depth":1,"text":"property using fwnode_irq_get_byname(), and route the interrupt"},{"depth":1,"text":"mappings to the matching register. When no interrupt-names are present,"},{"depth":1,"text":"default to INT1 to preserve the existing behaviour."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"Signed-off-by: Antoniu Miclaus <antoniu.miclaus@analog.com>"},{"depth":1,"text":"---"},{"depth":1,"text":"Changes in v2:"},{"depth":1,"text":"- Propagate -EPROBE_DEFER from fwnode_irq_get_byname()."},{"depth":1,"text":"- Drop the redundant irq return; the helper now only selects the INT map"},{"depth":1,"text":"  register."},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":" drivers/iio/accel/adxl367.c | 39 ++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++++---"},{"depth":1,"text":" 1 file changed, 36 insertions(+), 3 deletions(-)"},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"diff --git a/drivers/iio/accel/adxl367.c b/drivers/iio/accel/adxl367.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"index 8c3de11a10a3..df385740b17b 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"--- a/drivers/iio/accel/adxl367.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"+++ b/drivers/iio/accel/adxl367.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -13,6 +13,7 @@"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/iio/sysfs.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/interrupt.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/irq.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":"+#include <linux/property.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/regmap.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/regulator/consumer.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":" #include <linux/unaligned.h>"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -81,6 +82,7 @@"},{"depth":1,"text":" #define ADXL367_SAMPLES_L_MASK\t\tGENMASK(7, 0)"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":" #define ADXL367_REG_INT1_MAP\t\t0x2A"},{"depth":1,"text":"+#define ADXL367_REG_INT2_MAP\t\t0x2B"},{"depth":1,"text":" #define ADXL367_INT_INACT_MASK\t\tBIT(5)"},{"depth":1,"text":" #define ADXL367_INT_ACT_MASK\t\tBIT(4)"},{"depth":1,"text":" #define ADXL367_INT_FIFO_WATERMARK_MASK\tBIT(2)"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -168,6 +170,8 @@ struct adxl367_state {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tenum adxl367_odr\todr;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tenum adxl367_range\trange;"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tu8\t\tint_map_reg;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tunsigned int\tact_threshold;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tunsigned int\tact_time_ms;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tunsigned int\tinact_threshold;"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -366,7 +370,7 @@ static int adxl367_set_act_interrupt_en(struct adxl367_state *st,"},{"depth":1,"text":" {"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tunsigned int mask = adxl367_act_int_mask_tbl[act];"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-\treturn regmap_update_bits(st->regmap, ADXL367_REG_INT1_MAP,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\treturn regmap_update_bits(st->regmap, st->int_map_reg,"}],"lineCount":57,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t  mask, en ? mask : 0);"}],"lineCount":1,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Whilst here."},{"kind":"code","text":"\treturn regmap_assign_bits(st->regmap, st->int_map_reg, mask, en);"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"should do the job I think.  Maybe it is worth a precursor or follow up\npatch tidying up any other instances of this pattern in this driver.\n(Note I haven't actually checked if there are any!)"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -378,7 +382,7 @@ static int adxl367_get_act_interrupt_en(struct adxl367_state *st,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tunsigned int val;"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tint ret;"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"-\tret = regmap_read(st->regmap, ADXL367_REG_INT1_MAP, &val);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tret = regmap_read(st->regmap, st->int_map_reg, &val);"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tif (ret)"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\treturn ret;"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -401,7 +405,7 @@ static int adxl367_set_act_en(struct adxl367_state *st,"},{"depth":1,"text":" static int adxl367_set_fifo_watermark_interrupt_en(struct adxl367_state *st,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t\t\t   bool en)"},{"depth":1,"text":" {"},{"depth":1,"text":"-\treturn regmap_update_bits(st->regmap, ADXL367_REG_INT1_MAP,"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\treturn regmap_update_bits(st->regmap, st->int_map_reg,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t  ADXL367_INT_FIFO_WATERMARK_MASK,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t  en ? ADXL367_INT_FIFO_WATERMARK_MASK : 0);"}],"lineCount":19,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"regmap_assign_bits()"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1426,6 +1430,31 @@ static int adxl367_setup(struct adxl367_state *st)"},{"depth":1,"text":" \treturn adxl367_set_measure_en(st, true);"},{"depth":1,"text":" }"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+static int adxl367_set_int_map_reg(struct adxl367_state *st)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+{"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tint irq;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tirq = fwnode_irq_get_byname(dev_fwnode(st->dev), \"INT1\");"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tif (irq == -EPROBE_DEFER)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treturn irq;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tif (irq > 0) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tst->int_map_reg = ADXL367_REG_INT1_MAP;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tirq = fwnode_irq_get_byname(dev_fwnode(st->dev), \"INT2\");"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tif (irq == -EPROBE_DEFER)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treturn irq;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tif (irq > 0) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\tst->int_map_reg = ADXL367_REG_INT2_MAP;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t/* No interrupt-names: default to INT1 for backwards compatibility. */"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tst->int_map_reg = ADXL367_REG_INT1_MAP;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\treturn 0;"},{"depth":1,"text":"+}"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":" int adxl367_probe(struct device *dev, const struct adxl367_ops *ops,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t  void *context, struct regmap *regmap, int irq)"},{"depth":1,"text":" {"},{"depth":1,"text":"@@ -1482,6 +1511,10 @@ int adxl367_probe(struct device *dev, const struct adxl367_ops *ops,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tif (ret)"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\treturn ret;"},{"depth":1,"text":" "},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tret = adxl367_set_int_map_reg(st);"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\tif (ret)"},{"depth":1,"text":"+\t\treturn dev_err_probe(st->dev, ret, \"Failed to get interrupt\\n\");"},{"depth":1,"text":"+"},{"depth":1,"text":" \tret = devm_request_threaded_irq(st->dev, irq, NULL,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t\tadxl367_irq_handler, IRQF_ONESHOT,"},{"depth":1,"text":" \t\t\t\t\tindio_dev->name, indio_dev);"}],"lineCount":44,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":0,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"20260813081452.4289-4-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"},"20260816014959.18034ff6@jic23-huawei":{"id":"20260816014959.18034ff6@jic23-huawei","messageId":"20260816014959.18034ff6@jic23-huawei","references":["20260813081452.4289-1-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com","20260813081452.4289-4-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com","178671050969.21598.13163934753300429850.b4-review@b4"],"missingAncestorIds":["178671050969.21598.13163934753300429850.b4-review@b4","20260813081452.4289-4-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com","20260813081452.4289-1-antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"],"author":{"name":"Jonathan Cameron","address":"jic23@kernel.org"},"replyTo":[],"to":[{"name":"Nuno Sá","address":"nuno.sa@analog.com"}],"cc":[{"name":"Antoniu Miclaus","address":"antoniu.miclaus@analog.com"},{"name":"Marcelo Schmitt","address":"marcelo.schmitt@analog.com"},{"name":"Michael Hennerich","address":"Michael.Hennerich@analog.com"},{"name":"David Lechner","address":"dlechner@baylibre.com"},{"name":"Rob Herring","address":"robh@kernel.org"},{"name":"Krzysztof Kozlowski","address":"krzk+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"Conor Dooley","address":"conor+dt@kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-iio@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux@analog.com"},{"name":"","address":"devicetree@vger.kernel.org"},{"name":"","address":"linux-kernel@vger.kernel.org"}],"timestamp":{"raw":"2026-08-16T00:49:59.000Z","iso":"2026-08-16T00:49:59.000Z","valid":true},"subject":"Re: [PATCH v2 3/3] iio: accel: adxl367: add support for INT2 interrupt pin","mailingLists":[{"id":"devicetree.vger.kernel.org","displayName":"devicetree.vger.kernel.org"}],"blocks":[{"kind":"paragraph","text":"On Fri, 14 Aug 2026 13:28:29 +0100\nNuno Sá <nuno.sa@analog.com> wrote:"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":"On Thu, 13 Aug 2026 11:14:52 +0300, Antoniu Miclaus <antoniu.miclaus@analog.com> wrote:"},{"depth":1,"text":"> diff --git a/drivers/iio/accel/adxl367.c b/drivers/iio/accel/adxl367.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> index 8c3de11a10a3..df385740b17b 100644"},{"depth":1,"text":"> --- a/drivers/iio/accel/adxl367.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +++ b/drivers/iio/accel/adxl367.c"},{"depth":1,"text":"> @@ -1426,6 +1430,31 @@ static int adxl367_setup(struct adxl367_state *st)"},{"depth":1,"text":">  \treturn adxl367_set_measure_en(st, true);"},{"depth":1,"text":">  }"},{"depth":1,"text":">  "},{"depth":1,"text":"> +static int adxl367_set_int_map_reg(struct adxl367_state *st)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +{"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tint irq;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tirq = fwnode_irq_get_byname(dev_fwnode(st->dev), \"INT1\");"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tif (irq == -EPROBE_DEFER)"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\treturn irq;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\tif (irq > 0) {"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\tst->int_map_reg = ADXL367_REG_INT1_MAP;"},{"depth":1,"text":"> +\t\treturn 0;  "},{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"sashiko point is sensible but I guess both INT ouputs are pretty much"},{"depth":1,"text":"the same? So even even if there's a mismatch against spi/i2c I guess"},{"depth":1,"text":"it is not problematic?"}],"lineCount":23,"maximumDepth":1},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Sashiko has spotted a real problem here, be it one that won't\npass the binding restrictions which require INT1 to be first\nif it is present at all.  Anyhow we should be checking for a dts\nthat provides bother interrupts but ordered as INT2 INT1 then\nthe i2c and spi layers will give us the irq associated with\nthe first element (so INT2) but the code here will see that\nthere is an INT1 and route the interrupts there.  Hence the miss."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"If you are looking up interrupts by name you should use the\ninterrupt number retrieved. "},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"return irq from adxl367_set_int_map_reg() on success then"},{"kind":"code","text":"\tret = adxl367_set_int_map_reg(st);\n\tif (ret < 0)\n\t\treturn dev_err_probe(st->dev, ret, \"Failed to get interrupt\\n\");"},{"kind":"code","text":"\tirq = ret;\n\tret = devm_request_threaded_irq(st->dev, irq, NULL,\n\t\t\t\t\tadxl367_irq_handler, IRQF_ONESHOT,\n\t\t\t\t\tindio_dev->name, indio_dev);\n\tif (ret)\n\t\treturn dev_err_probe(st->dev, ret, \"Failed to request irq\\n\");"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Or pass it as a pointer so that adxl367_set_int_map_reg() can modify it\non matching by name. "},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Could argue that we should never see this but I think it's easy to harden\nagainst, so why not."},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Hmm. On a wide awake day I think I'd have spotted this, but not sure I would have\ntoday!"},{"kind":"paragraph","text":"Jonathan"},{"kind":"quote","lines":[{"depth":1,"text":""},{"depth":1,"text":"- Nuno Sá"},{"depth":1,"text":""}],"lineCount":3,"maximumDepth":1}],"patchIds":[],"attachmentMetadata":[],"sourceOrdinal":1,"diagnostics":[],"declaredParentMessageId":"178671050969.21598.13163934753300429850.b4-review@b4"}},"rootIds":["20260816013936.01f135dc@jic23-huawei","20260816014959.18034ff6@jic23-huawei"],"childrenByParent":{},"chronologicalIds":["20260816013936.01f135dc@jic23-huawei","20260816014959.18034ff6@jic23-huawei"],"patchSeries":[],"diagnostics":[],"patches":{}}}